Create one `{{ s.name }}ItemDefinition` asset per row above (see Install step 2)
and set its `effect` / `amount` / `targetId` fields to match.
{% if variant != "equipment" %}
`UseItem()` fires one matching event per effect — `OnHealEffect`,
`OnShieldEffect`, `OnStatBoostEffect`, `OnUnlockEffect`, `OnQuestFlagEffect` —
plus `OnItemUsed` for all of them. Subscribe from Health/Interactable/your own
scripts, or via `GameContext.Get<T>()` in a composed project: a composed
Health micro is auto-wired to `OnHealEffect` for you already. Composed stat boosts use an actor-owned modifier store: `speed` affects on-foot movement and AI movement, `armor` reduces incoming damage, and `aggression` expands guard sight range. Magnitudes are fractional (0.5 means +50%). Unsupported names or ambiguous actors log `[stat.abstain]`. Item effects have no authored duration; the runtime modifier API supports optional expiry and decay.
{% endif %}
